Webmachine
--------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a port. The HTTP state model it executes is Webmachine's, and
the name is used with the original authors' permission, on the one
condition they asked for: that the original be credited here.

Webmachine was written in Erlang at Basho Technologies:

    https://github.com/webmachine/webmachine

    %% @author Justin Sheehy <justin@basho.com>
    %% @author Andy Gross <andy@basho.com>
    %% @author Bryan Fink <bryan@basho.com>
    %% @copyright 2007-2014 Basho Technologies

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

webmachine-ruby is the Ruby port, and it is the one this tree was read
against:

    https://github.com/webmachine/webmachine-ruby

    Copyright 2011-2012 Sean Cribbs and contributors

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

What is theirs and not ours, named so the debt is legible rather than
implied:

  * The decision graph itself. Its specification here is
    webmachine-ruby's lib/webmachine/decision/flow.rb, node names and
    all - the B, C, D ... P and O nodes a reader of either project
    recognises.
  * The callback vocabulary and its defaults. resource_exists?,
    content_types_provided, is_authorized, generate_etag and the rest
    keep webmachine-ruby's names, arities and meanings, and a callback
    a resource does not define answers with webmachine-ruby's default.
  * The oracle this port is tested against. 74 cases of
    webmachine-ruby's own flow_spec run here, so "the same graph" is a
    claim under test rather than an intention.

Neither project is responsible for what this one does with any of it.

